# Day 15 - Connecting Git to GitHub

## 📚 Learning Objectives

* Learned how to connect a local repository to GitHub.
* Learned how git push uploads code to a remote repository.
* Learned the Git workflow.

## Git Commands Learned

### Change Directory

```bash
cd
```

Used to move between folders.

### Stage Changes

```bash
git add .
```

Used to add all modified files to the staging area.

### Create a Commit

```bash
git commit -m "message"
```

Used to save a snapshot of the project.

### Push to GitHub

```bash
git push
```

Used to upload commits to GitHub.

## Git Workflow

```text
Write Code
    ↓
git add .
    ↓
git commit
    ↓
git push
    ↓
GitHub
```

## Practical Work

* Created a writing folder.
* Wrote an article titled:

"Why I'm Learning to Code Every Single Day for a Year"

* Added the article to the repository.
* Learned how local code is uploaded to GitHub.

## Key Takeaways

* Git tracks changes locally.
* GitHub stores repositories remotely.
* git push uploads commits to GitHub.
* Consistency is more important than speed.
